## Category C: Color System & Severity

**8. Unify the traffic-light palette across charts, cards, and sidebar.**
The Design Review (rec A1) flagged: "CRITICAL renders as different reds (`#fb7185` / `#ef4444` / `#f87171`) across surfaces." Your token layer defines `--ow-bad:#f87171`. But Altair charts use `palette.BAD` which may differ from the token. Enforce: ONE hex per severity, referenced everywhere.

*Reasoning:* A DBA crossing from Alerts (card red) to the timeline (chart red) to the sidebar (indicator red) should see the SAME red. Three different reds subconsciously read as three different severities.

**9. Add colorblind-safe redundant encoding for severity.**
The Design Review (rec A2): "severity is color-only on the event timeline dots, KPI stripes, and sidebar." Add shape redundancy: CRITICAL=filled circle, HIGH=triangle, MEDIUM=open circle, LOW=dash. Use your SVG icons inline.

*Reasoning:* ~8% of males have some color vision deficiency. Red/amber on a dark background is the worst-case axis for deuteranopia. Shape is free and universal.

**10. The category color palette for charts needs stabilization at 5, not 8.**
Line 60-61: category range has 8 colors. But human perception reliably distinguishes ~5 categorical hues. The 6th-8th colors (`#a3e635`, palette.HIGH) are too close to existing entries under certain lighting. Cap at 5 and group the rest as "Other."

*Reasoning:* The "boss chart" problem from R1 persists in principle. Any chart with >5 series becomes confetti. A 5-color cap forces aggregation, which improves readability.

