## Category J: Export & Presentation

**34. Add a `@media print` stylesheet.**
There's no print styling. `Cmd+P` on any page renders Streamlit's sidebar, dark background, and interactive widgets — none of which belong on paper. Add: `@media print { sidebar: hidden; background: white; charts: rendered as static images; footer: timestamp + company. }`

*Reasoning:* Executives print things. Screenshots are the current workaround. A proper print stylesheet makes the app a self-contained report generator.

**35. Chart exports should include the chart title and takeaway text.**
When downloading a chart as PNG (Altair's built-in), only the chart renders — no title, no context, no timestamp. Wrap the chart in a container that includes the title bar and a "Generated by OVERWATCH, Aug 16 2026" footer.

*Reasoning:* A chart screenshot shared in Slack without context loses its meaning. A self-captioned chart carries its own explanation.

**36. Add "presentation mode" — full-screen, one-chart-at-a-time with click-to-advance.**
For boardroom presentations, the director wants: one big chart per screen, click to advance to the next metric. Currently they screenshot 8 charts and make a PowerPoint. A built-in presentation mode eliminates that workflow.

*Reasoning:* If your audience makes PowerPoints from your dashboards, you've failed to be the presentation tool. Cut out the intermediary.

